The Legend of Zelda breath of the wild  continues to surprise us with its wealth  of hidden secrets each new discovery  helps us better our understanding of its  massive world so to increase your  chances of survival we've compiled six  more handy tips you might not know  be wary there are potential spoilers  ahead if you enjoy this video like it  and subscribe to our YouTube channel for  more features on breath of the wild and  be sure to watch our previous videos and  all the things I wish I knew before I  started throughout your adventure you  often encounter gelatinous foes known as  choo-choos when you kill one it drops  choo choo jelly which doesn't do much  alone however if you hit one with an  elemental weapon or arrow you can change  its physical properties for example  shoot a choo-choo jelly with a fire  arrow and it will turn into a red  choo-choo jelly alternatively you can  drop 2 to jelly and freezing or burning  temperatures to change its element to  these special tutu jellies can be used  as handy environmental traps that you  can fool enemies into hitting which will  cause a small explosion that deals a  heavy dose of elemental damage  later on in your adventure he will  encounter silver versions of enemies  these pale skinned monsters are much  tougher than their lower ranked  counterparts so it's understandable if  you choose to avoid them but you're  missing out  silver enemies drop a lot of valuable  items when you defeat them  a silverback hablen for example drops a  hardy mix of items including the usual  blue cobbling horns and fangs as well as  valuable gems that you can't get from  weaker picaud leaves you're likely to go  through a few of your hard-earned  weapons trying to take down silver  enemies but they're valuable drops more  than make up for the effort it takes to  defeat them it can be overwhelming  exploring the Gerudo desert especially  if you don't have the tools and  equipment to deal with its blistering  heat while it's highly recommended to  consume a chilly elixir or equip armor  with heat resistance there are a couple  of interesting techniques you can  utilize to increase your chances of  survival you wouldn't think it but shape  can be a lifesaver if you're desperate  simply get under a rock and set up a  campfire and wait it out until the  weather gets cooler just make sure you  have the proper gear to deal with the  drop in temperature though if there's no  shade in sight and you're really  desperate you can always turn to any of  the deserts few bodies of water while  this technique helps to decrease your  body temperature it doesn't do so for  very long it's more of a last resort  than anything  the Thunder helm is a useful piece of  armor that gives you all the benefits of  a fully upgraded rubber armor suit in  addition it literally makes you immune  to lightning strikes with this  gold-plated helmet equipped you'll never  have to worry about thunderstorms or  electrical attacks ever again to earn  the Thunder helm complete every major  side quest in Gerudo town these can all  be found by talking to the town's  inhabitants once you've completed all  the side quests talk to read you insider  mansion and then she'll hand it over to  you dragon parts greatly enhanced the  effects of food and elixir recipes each  part type adds to the effect time of a  recipe but you'll want to focus  specifically on obtaining dragon horn  shards since they increase a recipe  effect timer to 30 minutes but where is  a good place to hunt dragon horn shards  easy head to the Rio last spring in the  Ferrand region before going stock up on  arrows and bring wood and Flint a fire  weapon is ideal if you have one also  shock-resistant armors or elixirs are a  must  anyway when you arrive make sure to  activate the shrine hidden inside the  nearby waterfall for future fast travel  next set up a campfire near Rio last  spring under this palm tree and wait out  until morning a dragon should emerge  from the water quickly take out your bow  and shoot at the dragon's horn a  successful shot will pop off a horn  shard for you to collect if one's not  enough simply relight your campfire and  repeat this process once you're  satisfied fast travel to a cooking pot  of your choice and throw in a dragon  horn shard along with ingredients from  your favorite recipe to get that sweet  half-hour bonus  a nifty way to heal yourself while  you're exploring Hyrule's mountainous  regions like Death Mountain or the  Hebrew mountains is jumping into their  hot springs the warm soothing waters  slowly heal you over time so take a  moment and sit back and relax and try to  think of the simpler times in your life  you know before you're defeated by a  calamity Ganon and all your friends died  which in turn caused the whole world to  be thrown into a state of doom and  uncertainty you know those times  ah refreshing isn't it what other cool  and useful mechanics have you found let  us know in the comments below and for  more coverage on the Legend of Zelda  breath of the wild be sure to subscribe  to our YouTube channel  [Music]
 

